{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q422473","formula":"C₁₀H₁₄N₅O₈P","hill":"C10H14N5O8P","elements":["H","C","N","O","P"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":14.0,"N":5.0,"O":8.0,"P":1.0},"names":{"en":"Guanosine monophosphate","ru":"Гуанозинмонофосфат"},"descriptions":{"en":"Guanosine monophosphate (GMP), also known as 5′-guanidylic acid or guanylic acid (conjugate base guanylate), is a nucleotide that is used as a monomer in RNA. It is an ester of phosphoric acid with the nucleoside guanosine. GMP consists of the phosphate group, the pentose sugar ribose, and the nucleobase guanine; hence it is a ribonucleotide monophosphate. Guanosine monophosphate is commercially produced by microbial fermentation.","ru":"Гуанозинмонофосфат, GMP, ГМФ, 5'-гуанидиловая кислота — нуклеотид, входящий в состав РНК. Это эфир фосфорной кислоты и гуанозинового нуклеозида. GMP состоит из фосфатной группы, сахара рибозы и азотистого основания гуанина."},"fame":32,"pubchemCid":135398631,"mass":363.22,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=NC2=C(N1[C@H]3[C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H](O3)COP(=O)(O)O)O)O)N=C(NC2=O)N","inchikey":"RQFCJASXJCIDSX-UUOKFMHZSA-N","iupac":"[(2R,3S,4R,5R)-5-(2-amino-6-oxo-1H-purin-9-yl)-3,4-dihydroxyoxolan-2-yl]methyl dihydrogen phosphate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"135398631","atoms":38,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.919,"y":0.251,"z":-1.692,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.056,"y":0.126,"z":-2.348,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.01,"y":0.559,"z":-1.464,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.45,"y":0.922,"z":-0.261,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.108,"y":0.707,"z":-0.411,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.1,"y":0.933,"z":0.612,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.206,"y":-0.048,"z":1.786,"el":"C"},{"x":0.786,"y":-1.13,"z":1.39,"el":"C"},{"x":1.891,"y":-0.296,"z":0.753,"el":"C"},{"x":1.216,"y":0.75,"z":0.023,"el":"O"},{"x":2.772,"y":-1.107,"z":-0.193,"el":